{id:'ch11-pg-2',title:'Typical application',level:'foundation',kind:'classification',q:'Which is a typical plate-girder application identified in the chapter?',choices:['Long-span bridge or heavy gantry girder','Light curtain wall only','Timber roof batten only','Nonstructural partition'],answer:0,explanation:'Plate girders are common in bridges, gantry girders, power-plant structures and other heavy-load applications.',source:S},
{id:'ch11-pg-3',title:'Modern fabrication',level:'core',kind:'recognition',q:'How are modern plate girders predominantly assembled?',choices:['By welding','By casting the complete girder as one steel block','By gluing timber laminations','By prestressing concrete only'],answer:0,explanation:'The textbook describes modern plate girders as predominantly welded built-up members.',source:S},
{id:'ch11-pg-4',title:'Haunched form',level:'core',kind:'reasoning',q:'Why might a plate girder be tapered or haunched?',choices:['To vary depth where force demand or geometry justifies it','To make the steel modulus larger near supports','To prevent all shear','To avoid using flanges'],answer:0,explanation:'Fabrication permits variation in depth to better follow structural demand or geometric constraints.',source:S},
{id:'ch11-pg-5',title:'Force matching',level:'application',kind:'reasoning',q:'What is the structural benefit of varying a fabricated cross-section along the span?',choices:['Material can be placed more closely in proportion to changing force demand','The load combination is removed','The web need not carry shear','Deflection becomes zero'],answer:0,explanation:'A varying section can improve material efficiency by responding to changing moments and shears.',source:S},
{id:'ch11-pg-6',title:'Rolled versus fabricated',level:'retrieval',kind:'concept',q:'Which statement best distinguishes a plate girder from a standard rolled I-section?',choices:['The plate girder is assembled from separate plates and can be custom proportioned','The plate girder cannot resist bending','The rolled section has no web','Only the plate girder uses steel'],answer:0,explanation:'The defining advantage is custom fabrication of the web and flanges.',source:S}
