{id:'ch11-stress-5',title:'Efficient division of roles',level:'application',kind:'reasoning',q:'Why is a deep thin web with substantial flanges structurally efficient?',choices:['The web supplies depth and shear area while flanges place bending material far from the neutral axis','The web removes all bending moment','The flanges remove all shear force from equilibrium','The arrangement changes steel modulus'],answer:0,explanation:'The cross-section exploits the different stress distributions of bending and shear.',source:S},
{id:'ch11-stress-6',title:'Proportioning clue',level:'retrieval',kind:'concept',q:'Which simple design allocation follows from the chapter stress-distribution discussion?',choices:['Flanges mainly for bending; web mainly for shear','Web mainly for bending; stiffeners mainly for axial tension','Flanges only for shear; web only for torsion','Welds carry all global actions'],answer:0,explanation:'This division of roles is the central starting point for plate-girder proportioning.',source:S}
